course: dictionary
lesson: 5898
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word mara is one of them. Its meaning depends on the sentence. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning is right.
explain: A mara is an animal from South America. It looks like a small deer or a long-legged hare, but it is a rodent, a relative of the guinea pig. Read this: «The mara is a rodent that lives on the grassy plains of Patagonia.» Here mara means an animal.
explain: The Mara is also a name. It is a river and an area in Kenya and Tanzania, and the Masai Mara is a famous wildlife reserve. Read this: «The great migration is real: over a million wildebeest move round the Serengeti and Masai Mara every year.» Here Masai Mara means a place, not an animal. A capital letter at the start is a clue that it is a name.
explain: Mara is also a girl's name. How do you know which meaning is right? Read the rest of the sentence. If it talks about a person, it is a name. If it talks about a river, a reserve or a wild animal, it is a place or an animal. Always check by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A mara is a South American animal and a relative of the guinea pig.
fact: A mara looks like a small deer or a long-legged hare, but it is a rodent.
fact: The Mara is a river and area in Kenya and Tanzania.
fact: The Masai Mara is a famous wildlife reserve.
fact: Mara is also a girl's name.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning. The sentence tells you which one is right.
fact: A capital letter in the middle of a sentence often means a name of a person or a place.
exercise: «The mara is a rodent that lives in South America.» What kind of animal is a mara? | A big cat with spots | A fish from a river | *A rodent, a relative of the guinea pig | A bird that cannot fly
exercise: «Each year more than a million wildebeest follow the rain round the Serengeti and the Masai Mara.» What is the Masai Mara? | A South American animal | *A famous wildlife reserve | A type of wildebeest | A rainy season
exercise: «Mara and her brother went to the zoo on Saturday.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Mara? | An animal | A river | *A girl's name
exercise: Read this: «The Mara is a river and area in Kenya and Tanzania.» What is the Mara? | A rodent from Patagonia | A girl who lives in Kenya | *A river and area in Kenya and Tanzania | A kind of guinea pig
test: What does a mara look like? | A tiny fish with fins | A big cat with stripes | A bird with very long wings | *A small deer or a long-legged hare
test: Why does «Masai Mara» start with capital letters? | Because it is a girl's name | *Because it is a name of a place | Because it is a type of animal | Because it is the start of a sentence every time
exam: In «the Masai Mara is a famous wildlife reserve», what does Masai Mara mean? | *A famous wildlife reserve | A type of wildebeest | A kind of rain | A large mountain
